  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Narratives of violence: the impact of internal displacement on violence against women in Nepal and Myanmar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Myanmar and Nepal are countries in transition. Both have recently emerged from long-term civil conflicts, and their populations have been afflicted by natural disasters. As a result these two countries have seen rates of internal displacement among the highest in the world (e.g. in 2015, 9200 per 100,000 residents in Nepal, and 3000 per 100,000 in Myanmar). We will document women&apos;s explanations of how displacement has affected gendered relations and women&apos;s resultant experiences of violence. This will involve collecting unstructured narratives and quantitative data from women who have experienced rural-urban displacement.</narrative>
  </description>
